+       already-open input against the intended output by `st_dev`/`st_ino`, which is what
+       catches `--out-dir .`, an absolute DIR that contains the operand, and a hard link — all
+       three are the same file by identity and none is the same path string (research.md R21).
+       It must run *before* the open, because `O_TRUNC` truncates during `os.open` itself:
+       there is no "open then notice" (FR-036, SR-012).
+    2. **Open.** `os.open(out_path, O_WRONLY|O_CREAT|O_TRUNC|O_NOFOLLOW, 0o600)` discharges four
+       requirements in one call with no check-then-act window (research.md R20):
