+       the case an existence check would miss and the one that would otherwise silently write
+       redacted data outside DIR (SR-010); `0o600` sets owner-only permissions as the file is
+       created, and because a mode argument applies only on creation, a pre-existing file keeps
+       exactly the mode its owner gave it (SR-011); `O_CREAT` without `O_EXCL` together with
+       `O_TRUNC` replaces an existing file's content in full, leaving no remnant (FR-026).
